          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %p Other rings of generalized power series include:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Novikov+field"} Novikov field
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ribenboim+power+series"} Ribenboim power series
          %p
            Hahn series are a special kind of Ribenboim power series, but Puiseux and Novikov series are not. However, they are all instances of the linearization of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finiteness+space"} finiteness space
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              wikipedia
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puiseux_series"} Puiseux series
          %p
            The sketched proof of theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Puiseux"}
            was extracted from notes on a seminar by Boyarchenko on local class field theory:
          %ul
            %li
              Mitya Boyarchenko, Kottwitz Seminar Lectures, (U. Michigan, Winter 2011). (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/seminars/kottwitz/HieuNgoLocalCFT.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and the reader may refer to the classic text by Serre for a fuller treatment:
          %ul
            %li
              Jean-Pierre Serre,
              %em Local Fields
              (trans. Marvin J. Greenberg), Graduate Texts in Math. 67, Springer 1980.
          %p For a noncommutative generalization see
          %ul
            %li
              D. Grigoriev,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Analogue of Newton-Puiseux series for non-holonomic D-modules and factoring
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 9
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://logic.pdmi.ras.ru/~grigorev/pub/puiseux_journal.pdf"} pdf
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preblob/3537"} pdf
          %p Other references
          %ul
            %li
              Jan Kiwi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Puiseux series dynamics of Quadratic rational maps
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.0059"} arxiv/1106.0059
            %li
              Luis Felipe Tabera,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On real tropical bases and real tropical discriminants
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2211"} arxiv/1311.2211
          %blockquote
            %p We explore the concept of real tropical basis of an ideal in the field of real Puiseux series. We show explicit tropical bases of zero-dimensional real radical ideals, linear ideals and hypersurfaces coming from combinatorial patchworking. But we also show that there exist real radical ideals that do not admit a tropical basis. As an application, we show how to compute the set of singular points of a real tropical hypersurface. i.e. we compute the real tropical discriminant.
          %ul
            %li
              Evelia García Barroso, Pedro Daniel González Pérez, Patrick Popescu-Pampu,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Variations on inversion theorems for Newton-Puiseux series
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1606.08029"} arxiv/1606.08029
